    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6361" root="جمل" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَمَّالٌ</span></b>  <i>An owner,</i> or <i>an attendant, of a camel</i>
or <i>camels:</i> (KL, TA: * [see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جامِلٌ</span>:]) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَمَّالَةٌ</span> <i>owners,</i> or <i>attendants, of camels;</i> (S, K,
TA;) similar to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَيَّالَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَمَّارَةٌ</span>; (S, TA;) as
the former is to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَمَّارٌ</span>. (TA.) [See an ex. of the
latter in a verse cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِذَا</span>.]

